#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "00b0d838-163d-5299-beaf-255f9b13cf71" :question/math-academy-id "e-11034" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, x^2+y^2 \\geq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A - \\partial A = \\textrm{int}\\, A$\n\n- $\\textrm{int}\\, A \\cap \\partial A = \\emptyset$\n\n- $A = \\textrm{int}\\,A \\cup \\partial A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/2c/2c7e7ac1b320591250b045ebe493b28e0bb9cdb38469324ee496aacb8766c75b.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\textrm{int}\\, A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = A - \\partial A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/49/49ffc47c2ae1cde5e93e8607db8ef6b58eb7938913f82ea41f281df1fe334c14.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\textrm{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A - \\partial A = \\textrm{int}\\, A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\textrm{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\textrm{int}\\, A \\cap \\partial A = \\emptyset,$ where $\\emptyset$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A = \\textrm{int}\\,A \\cup \\partial A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "a8045dd8-90b8-5671-9003-2539c502cb49" :question/math-academy-id "e-11035" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\,  y^2 - 1 \\leq  x , \\, -2 \\leq y \\leq  2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}, \\, -2 <     y <     2\\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/1c/1ca3afd22a68f2ce8b29645879967c3d130d5c19a7d529296ff129eb92693295.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\textrm{int}\\, A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = A - \\partial A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/6e/6e7f7a326a89c60bbc11e48d491ed05a176161881368f189aec7aad916752b64.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{y^2 - 1 < x}, \\, -2 <     y <     2\\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "44971e25-0367-5b13-a6be-db503c6b4539" :question/math-academy-id "e-12399" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{(x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 : x^2+y^2 -1<0\\}\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\partial A = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,: \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}} \\, \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\\partial A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\\partial A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/8d/8d3c7549948f0dd0f6a634526f1d978ae69d0c5b25611981b63a7cf389608087.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the circle $x^2+y^2 = 1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\partial A = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, \\bbox[5px, border: 1px solid black]{x^2+y^2 = 1} \\, \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3243b0c1-092b-5601-b0a7-3f3c3e1a11a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238491} {:answer/id #uuid "3292f4f8-3340-5dcc-8508-318774f90133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238495} {:answer/id #uuid "99e00a77-24b1-59aa-8b87-eeed024a6ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\le x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239391} {:answer/id #uuid "bc38a932-011d-51ce-8574-ad8d957e354d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239697} {:answer/id #uuid "ed989251-9ebe-5e5b-b96b-de3e3996d705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3292f4f8-3340-5dcc-8508-318774f90133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238495} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5caea72-1771-5754-bf55-8da480cdcb1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47ef764e-19dd-5c12-b6a9-8ee51c79b104" :question/math-academy-id "q-105176" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0<y\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<1\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c7/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0542e243-f002-5e39-8f10-7dabe8842be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275523} {:answer/id #uuid "0874fc66-9829-550a-a0b4-b7df5d59c4ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275552} {:answer/id #uuid "3e066485-16c6-558f-a647-7f8e654d14d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276014} {:answer/id #uuid "444f0095-6ceb-5176-b83d-e73abef5e8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276080} {:answer/id #uuid "74d929ec-a574-5787-9e4e-a920d01d5a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e066485-16c6-558f-a647-7f8e654d14d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276014} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cb5f4b3-f548-5bf9-a994-4b652192dbe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1eb8e242-f7cb-5632-a09c-62dcc98103d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161445" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee6d693-f4d6-580b-9964-9fc00eb004d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275605} {:answer/id #uuid "1028a7f0-5258-520e-90ee-5b63d0356e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}>16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275618} {:answer/id #uuid "8189729c-0629-50b6-92d0-d418c4f820e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276644} {:answer/id #uuid "b7ef749f-1c2e-5b6a-939b-383c25cc4d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277109} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c6d05f-7e9c-5248-b9af-2af6ca3f639a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\ge 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ee6d693-f4d6-580b-9964-9fc00eb004d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275605} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9817895-bacc-54a6-8df7-a5eb8c487a12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5a4373e-6e45-5815-aca4-6d44f34a430e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161590" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b1/b1074330fc650cf6af682f173f50943d779819afa59bf5be19edb88def1ef03a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158838e0-efdb-532f-9f9b-a61b3d97ab19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\ge -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398550} {:answer/id #uuid "ff58ee15-73c1-5580-9e71-8bba76a9b817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\le -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398551} {:answer/id #uuid "7091d7cf-fb36-5a53-885a-a308985da886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}<-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398552} {:answer/id #uuid "d659a207-f68e-587b-a239-ea9f4042aefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398553} {:answer/id #uuid "a4015647-d62f-51c8-aff3-60d6eea64e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}>-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d659a207-f68e-587b-a239-ea9f4042aefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398553} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c536b1b-39ee-59d3-8fef-dfde6d2dc504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28ca8dae-bb66-5179-8a04-f47a13f5a86d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161596" :question/problem "![](images/2b/2bb25857047d7a0200d4c58ee3756b0efa0f2d13aaca8664b1fe49414c18a461.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e217ad3d-748d-5af0-96b1-e1ce473458d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398557} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0bfd32-77d4-5a28-b13f-6b03980aac88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}>36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398558} {:answer/id #uuid "d591b7a8-1678-5fc4-8efb-59323697512e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398559} {:answer/id #uuid "b121b495-13d7-5ac2-843d-1f8022ddb37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398560} {:answer/id #uuid "b5797dbb-800e-55ff-b8bd-e000ab812acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\ge 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d591b7a8-1678-5fc4-8efb-59323697512e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398559} :answer-field/id #uuid "634120e7-888a-527b-b321-8e6ce84d2f2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcfdd46f-14ab-5535-a276-fcd0db509adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161598" :question/problem "![](images/11/112ab676fa5a97db198a872c33579900deab76e0c3c9c92016e165a67482bbcd.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/44/44f3a2a8e535c7248dac49d126da9bf17fce94c357f15c93a3eaad665e73b47a.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1492c819-223a-51aa-8419-2068e9f77a47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y>{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275669} {:answer/id #uuid "32d5055f-5b6f-5079-bd6f-f6898cbde28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y\\le {x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275929} {:answer/id #uuid "cf193ff5-eeeb-556d-95c4-a4282f4e52b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y\\ge {x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277309} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c1eed7-7497-5711-bf73-42a47d85ccf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y<{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277360} {:answer/id #uuid "e752c7da-66cd-5818-9c1c-9035abb465e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y={x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e752c7da-66cd-5818-9c1c-9035abb465e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y={x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277499} :answer-field/id #uuid "014c1750-803a-5f30-b2fb-c1a2eda5174c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fba7584d-6a44-58f1-91c4-4ca141af635a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161599" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y\\ge {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0fc95ee69ce7121c0cf8ae68029b135d9667f50275227d141f1d979f85408859.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the  parabola $-2y={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y={x}^{2}\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06342551-0e88-5a6b-bd0d-60e7e94f92cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275532} {:answer/id #uuid "514cdd25-4769-5166-850c-a323f4ce90d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276204} {:answer/id #uuid "9472a39b-33fc-53d0-8cc5-e0e82c1a530a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276820} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d437f7-5a15-5e16-8d18-d6085aacba13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276973} {:answer/id #uuid "e15fd5f3-6d8f-5ca6-a7db-f5eec29b87ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06342551-0e88-5a6b-bd0d-60e7e94f92cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275532} :answer-field/id #uuid "0377995e-0aa9-5059-b2c1-6fd8c5abf106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2307ae9e-a249-5090-bfed-df0660f7b0eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161601" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ff/ff1f735266f66879834e02ca7601e90e40dfa7929e5796d4a3f8cb4ff2828de7.png)\n\n  \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd3c14e6-cdac-5b50-83d2-c7a7e936d3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378852} {:answer/id #uuid "7e056cb0-ca61-54f2-a5e9-73842a82ebde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378853} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cb356d-0a4a-57bd-9dbf-4365785bf3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378854} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fe1489-c5d9-51b7-a695-df2f0bfed8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378855} {:answer/id #uuid "301c3c2d-1689-5485-a99c-8b0d727eadbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3c14e6-cdac-5b50-83d2-c7a7e936d3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378852} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fce85d8-31bd-5894-a084-f12d40765a2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cfd8147-c3e0-5cab-9b14-cee4034ac307" :question/math-academy-id "q-161623" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51545767-3cc2-5437-9f48-638348ea4cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276205} {:answer/id #uuid "65e476b0-8d46-5284-adff-7ab3dfc01d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276391} {:answer/id #uuid "8a5f5c40-cedb-5337-a6d5-fdb5d40c8667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276728} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbc21fd-75c6-57b1-b5df-f0a1cd6cf1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277540} {:answer/id #uuid "fbea97be-23e3-55aa-9854-424f79b2abcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65e476b0-8d46-5284-adff-7ab3dfc01d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276391} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c6778a-20db-511f-af8b-42a6afc7a710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be0484aa-ac87-5330-9ede-cd54e1386a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-161625" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cdca164d343d8bff4c78a1e366e52c588ca6c54dfdea61acea1900bcbdc79f31.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and II are false. As we have seen, $A$ contains all its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3224235d-c85f-581e-b0a5-fa619bf3e2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378873} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec09210-3416-5440-a20c-8e780f2effa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378874} {:answer/id #uuid "2180dbea-78a1-57c5-87db-f486a6914b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378875} {:answer/id #uuid "3257f157-5b66-55fe-830a-873790844a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378876} {:answer/id #uuid "7789b753-b1d3-5748-ae54-82d9e789e198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ec09210-3416-5440-a20c-8e780f2effa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6419e7cc-8024-5bbd-a920-bed8d2a11d14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e963f0b-a2c7-5ae0-844a-f3e405d79aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161649" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$\n- $A⊂\\text{int}A$\n- $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/649c33f1738a35f3d298038bd2cf05d3b435424a4efbbb1e6143cf0d56b2bfd6.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A⊈\\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-\\text{int}A=∂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1325c53d-2a90-5778-afb8-06fcd3205174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278766} {:answer/id #uuid "4728e048-8ecd-5ccd-ac4b-e6cbd5e27ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279227} {:answer/id #uuid "6578e51f-39ed-5919-8a55-dbd0a80e7410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279513} {:answer/id #uuid "789e155f-7ca8-5285-8b89-650ea79f4175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279665} {:answer/id #uuid "ae570040-33fc-5a0b-b3dd-7a737099d6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1325c53d-2a90-5778-afb8-06fcd3205174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278766} :answer-field/id #uuid "07fc9cff-ef6e-56b5-99d9-20afa2b43a94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82618995-8e73-5f87-bf17-79a78614a421" :question/math-academy-id "q-161700" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<x<1}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d6/d60700d57ddc72bb410b3136f546705676f83d23d9071ffe972c5163d11af549.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/75/75e0132cd3854f18e9ab409b7fd13af3898f78b5174647bf2b33b8438b9228cb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "388d2b25-435c-5296-9aa6-b2d86268ab07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y\\le x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401270} {:answer/id #uuid "f7697d7e-3437-54cb-8f6c-2a92ca54ced0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\le y\\le x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401271} {:answer/id #uuid "715a11d5-48d4-58bf-b2c8-7bc968bb12ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\le y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401272} {:answer/id #uuid "6585c463-6545-5cb0-b223-cfd5eb13f4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401273} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc09c1e-549e-5605-9dc7-40a23cf11591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6585c463-6545-5cb0-b223-cfd5eb13f4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x<y<x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401273} :answer-field/id #uuid "41473911-1989-5683-9728-285b3c146754" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cae3814-ea99-54e9-86e7-c0bc019bdf37" :question/math-academy-id "q-161718" :question/problem "![](images/af/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c